    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d375">

                <pb facs="0579" n="491" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg491"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Grubb.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-03-14"><hi rendition="#italic">March 14,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 193.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 210, of the 13th ultimo, in the matter of the prohibition of American pork
                    in the new Spanish tariff, and your efforts to effect its removal.</p>
                <p>The Department commends your earnest and constant attention to this important
                    subject, and hopes to learn at an early date that this unjust prohibition has
                    been removed, as you expect it soon will be.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
